# SRG-APP-000516-AU-000380  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must be configured with the organization-defined
# severity or criticality levels of each event that is being sent from
# individual devices or hosts.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000516-AU-000380
group:           V-206517
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000366
control_rev5:    CM-6

contribution:    Splunk can carry a severity value on each alert it raises, so the
                 organization's own criticality levels are expressed in the application's
                 configuration rather than assigned by hand after the fact.

governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [] alert.severity present

external:        The criticality levels themselves and the mapping of event to level, which
                 the check takes from the site's system security plan.
external:        Severity or facility values that each sending device stamps on its own
                 records before transmission, carried by that device.

citation:        Central Log Server SRG SRG-APP-000516-AU-000380 check text;
                 savedsearches.conf.spec:887 (alert.severity = <integer>, valid values 1
                 through 6, default 3); props.conf.spec:80 ([<spec>] stanza forms)
finding:         Alerts carry no severity value, so the application does not express the
                 organization's criticality levels for the events it receives from
                 individual devices and hosts.
